<title>UK: Scholl sells French cosmetics division.</title>
<headline>Scholl sells French cosmetics division.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Scholl Plc said on Thursday that it had sold its French cosmetics business Laboratoires Valdor SA to a group of private investors for eight million francs.</p>
<p>Out of that consideration, five million francs are payable on completion of the deal with the balance payable in three annual instalments of one million francs.</p>
<p>Valdor's sales in 1995 stood at 8.6 million stg.</p>
<p>This sale follows Scholl's disposal last week of cleansing product brand Septivon to Chefaro International BV of France for 125 million francs.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
